WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:03.040
- [Interviewer] All right, Alison.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:03.873
- Yeah.

00:00:03.873 --> 00:00:04.832
- [Interviewer] Allison,
where are you from?

00:00:04.832 --> 00:00:05.760
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.080
- I grew up in Bryan, Ohio.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.000
- And tell me about your family.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.384
You had both your parents
growing up as a kid?

00:00:11.384 --> 00:00:13.960
- No, I lived with my mom.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.130
My parents got divorced
when I was about four

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.130
and my mom moved just around
from town to town in Ohio

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.292
with her husband she had.

00:00:24.292 --> 00:00:26.280
(Allison chuckles)

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.053
- [Interviewer] And how would
you describe your childhood?

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.230
- It was pretty normal up
until towards my teenage years

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.670
then it started getting really abusive

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.253
'cause my mom married someone
that didn't like me very much,

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.460
and I ended up running away
from home when I was 16

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.930
and I never went back.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.730
- [Interviewer] Did
you finish high school?

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.260
- No. I dropped out halfway
through my sophomore year.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.953
- [Interviewer] And what
kind of teenager were you?

00:00:53.198 --> 00:00:56.390
- I was a pretty normal
teenager I was really shy

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.760
not really outgoing at all.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.890
I did sports but mostly did it just

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.610
'cause there was nothing else to do.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.510
My town only had like 200 people in it.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.500
- [Interviewer] Oh, small town.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.250
- Yeah. So being different wasn't really

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.473
part of the itinerary.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:14.080
So I tried to like mingle
as much as possible.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.530
And when it just got too
rough I just up and left.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.970
- [Interviewer] When you
say different, you mean?

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.169
- Oh I was a gay boy back then.

00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:24.230
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.330
- But I didn't really
like identify as a gay boy

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.183
I just like to identify as Adam,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.510
and I wouldn't really
figure out what I really was

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.421
until like 10 years later.

00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:39.254
- [Interviewer] Oh really?

00:01:39.254 --> 00:01:41.563
- Yeah. And that was
about three years ago.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:43.860
- [Interviewer] So this
is all fairly recent

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.670
that you realized who you are?

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.310
- Yeah, I used to actually
hate transgenders.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.629
I thought they were
disgusting little creatures-

00:01:51.629 --> 00:01:52.462
- [Interviewer] Really?

00:01:52.462 --> 00:01:54.005
(Allison laughs)

00:01:54.005 --> 00:01:56.713
- Yeah but I guess it was just
because I wanted to be them

00:01:56.713 --> 00:01:57.650
and didn't know how to-

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.200
- [Interviewer] Yeah. There's
some interesting crossover

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.310
between people who hate transgenders

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.720
and those that are transgender.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:04.553
- Yeah.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.690
- [Interviewer] It's a blurred line.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.574
- Very much so.

00:02:07.574 --> 00:02:09.649
(Allison chuckles)

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:11.716
- [Interviewer] And you
came to California when?

00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:14.683
- First time I moved
to California I was 18,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.500
and I moved all around the United States

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.210
but I always ended up
coming back it was actually

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.110
like my 28th time living here.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.910
It's the longest stint
I've ever lived here

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.510
but yeah, I came here for a rave.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.990
(Allison chuckles)

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:31.823
- [Interviewer] And stayed?

00:02:31.823 --> 00:02:33.663
- The first time yeah, from Utah.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.840
- [Interviewer] Did you find
that being transgender out here

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.800
is a little more accepted
than back in small town Ohio?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.470
- Well I've never actually went back,

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.623
I haven't seen anyone in my
family since I was 16 yeah.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.290
The atmosphere is different,

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.680
I wouldn't say I'm more accepted

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.290
because sometimes I wish
I was still a gay boy

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.690
with the means how people interact with me

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:05.690
and how not accepted it
is really is really is.

00:03:07.022 --> 00:03:07.855
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:03:07.855 --> 00:03:09.910
- Especially in the area that I live in.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.820
- [Interviewer] You still get
roughed up and treated badly?

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.690
- Yeah. I mean on a daily
basis it's gotten really,

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.070
really bad actually I don't know why,

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.020
but I don't do anything to antagonize it

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:25.020
it's just me being there
and it's just it's weird.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.400
It's just really weird.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.520
- [Interviewer] Yeah. Now
there's a lot of drugs

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.810
in this neighborhood are
you involved in any of that?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.973
- I am. I started doing
Crystal when I was 16,

00:03:38.663 --> 00:03:42.850
wasn't until I started shooting
up about seven years ago

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.640
that I became homeless and I was homeless

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:50.640
for like four years, got clean
and then started doing Black

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.420
and then eventually moved on to Fentanyl.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.130
- [Interviewer] So now
you're using Fentanyl?

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:55.963
- Yeah.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.690
- [Interviewer] And Crystal, Meth as well?

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:01.093
- I use Crystal mostly for work.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.400
- [Interviewer] So your work is?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.290
- The Blade.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.580
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
So you go over to the-

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.810
- No, not anymore I go up to Santa Monica.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.643
- [Interviewer] Boulevard?

00:04:11.643 --> 00:04:12.760
- Yeah, there's more money up there.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.593
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.713
It's probably the bottom

00:04:15.713 --> 00:04:17.930
of the barrel money down here.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.920
- Yeah they want 20 bucks for everything.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.370
(Allison laughs)

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.540
- [Interviewer] And on
Santa Monica, Boulevard,

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.240
you can make how much?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.810
- Well I used to be able
to make on a weekday

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.620
like three to $500 and on a weekend like

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.000
it's pretty much no cap on the weekends.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.830
It's anywhere between a 100
bucks to like 800 bucks,

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.080
a night.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:43.318
But now with the pandemic
it's just there's nights

00:04:43.318 --> 00:04:44.460
where I don't make anything.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:45.350
- [Interviewer] Oh really?

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.600
- Yeah. 'Cause there's no one out there.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.580
- [Interviewer] Yeah I know. I understand.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.980
But before the COVID thing broke out

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.170
what was your typical customer like?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:01.430
- Mostly places. I don't
date black guys not

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:02.340
'cause I'm racist just

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.340
cause I've had very negative interactions,

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:13.950
and a lot of guys from the
studios is what I prefer

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.820
oddly enough I don't like to
get into cars really nice cars

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.610
because they generally don't
have a lot of cash on hand

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:26.580
and they wanna do things
before they pay me

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.100
and then they end up
paying me like nothing.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.690
So that's happened like once or twice

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.890
so I'd rather get in a car
that's like all wrinkety

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.890
'cause they have cash on hand and yeah

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:42.890
so basically it's the
lower class is my clients

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.170
because they generally are the only ones

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:48.190
that they don't have banks
so all their money's on hand.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.060
- [Interviewer] They have cash on them?

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.650
- Yeah, you can work 'em out of it.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.880
(Allison laughs)

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.630
- [Interviewer] And have you
had bad experiences doing this?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.070
- I had way bad experiences
there was one time I got

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:02.120
hospitalized because i don't
really know what happened

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.610
I just remember getting in the car

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.403
and then waking up on the pavement.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.030
And I think he sucker
punched me in the face.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.070
- [Interviewer] Rough you up?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.850
- Yeah, but he left all my money

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:16.190
and he left me on the
sidewalk with all my stuff

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.850
so I think that's just how he got off.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:18.780
- [Interviewer] He just
wanted to beat you up

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:22.803
- Yeah. And I've dealt
with a few guys like that.

00:06:25.091 --> 00:06:26.250
- [Interviewer] Do you
get arrested sometimes?

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.590
- I've never gotten arrested

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.170
but I date one of the cops over here.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.760
So he pretty much said he gave me

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.970
out of anything as long
as it's not a felony.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:34.803
- [Interviewer] That's nice.

00:06:34.803 --> 00:06:36.410
- Yeah.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.350
- [Interviewer] What is the
hardest part of your lifestyle?

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.233
Is it the danger?

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:46.087
- The hardest part is just
sometimes it's just walking

00:06:46.087 --> 00:06:48.978
out the door 'cause you knew
that something's gonna happen.

00:06:48.978 --> 00:06:50.870
- [Interviewer] Is it the
self-esteem hit that you take?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.670
- Yeah. I used to have
really high self-esteem

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.620
when I first started it was empowering.

00:06:57.142 --> 00:06:58.520
It was the kind of thing that I never got

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.570
when I came out of the
closet as being gay,

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.880
and so that empowering
feeling is just kind

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:07.730
of slowly been dwindled down
to where like it takes longer

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:08.963
to get out that door.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.410
- [Interviewer] And what
emotions do you deal with mostly?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.620
Is it anxiety?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.610
Is it anger?

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:15.820
Is it depression?

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.960
- It's awkwardness.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.690
Like that's just pretty
much what I deal with

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.590
'cause I don't wanna be awkward
but people make me awkward.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:24.423
- [Interviewer] You feel awkward?

00:07:24.423 --> 00:07:27.393
- Yeah. And I just wanna be normal.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.193
- [Interviewer] Do you have any friends?

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.370
- I have a friend.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.250
- [Interviewer] Good friends?

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.980
- I have one good friend in Long Beach.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.720
He's the one that helped
me off the streets.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.980
He used to be a counselor
at the McIntosh House

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.560
or Mc Intyre House.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.940
And yeah, he helped me.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:50.800
He helped me by not helping
me, by cutting me off

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.590
'cause he used to be my connect.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.560
And, then he just kind of like

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.930
he's been the most
stable person in my life

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.670
since before I ran away.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:05.293
So, yeah he's the only person
I would consider a friend.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.500
- [Interviewer] And these
interactions with the guys

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.230
that you pick up how do they go?

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.580
Are they just quick?

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:16.060
- Yeah. Once they bust their gun.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:16.998
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:08:16.998 --> 00:08:18.260
(Allison laughs)

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.963
How many of those do you do in a night?

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.183
- On a good night I'll
do like eight or 12,

00:08:24.572 --> 00:08:26.860
but on a slow night
it's like five at least.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.470
I won't get off the
Blade unless I have five.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:31.493
- [Interviewer] Do you recall
your first time doing this?

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.110
- I think so. I remember being awkward.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.131
I was not a girl

00:08:37.131 --> 00:08:38.980
(Allison laughs)

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:39.940
but it's actually

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.760
what got me into being trans

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.130
and realizing that that's who I was,

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.260
was because girls made
more money on the Blade,

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.510
than any other gender.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:54.150
So it's what got me being
comfortable with it.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.700
I used to runaway when the sun came out

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.499
and put on my boy clothes and-

00:08:57.499 --> 00:08:59.220
(Allison laughs)

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.616
- [Interviewer] A lot of
the guys that pick you up

00:09:00.616 --> 00:09:02.193
on the download you think?

00:09:02.193 --> 00:09:04.193
- Some of them are, some of them aren't,

00:09:05.448 --> 00:09:07.600
they're mostly all drug users.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.940
Like, Oh, I don't know if I could say this

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.400
I don't wanna say it

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.714
but I have a really high profile client.

00:09:13.714 --> 00:09:14.815
- [Interviewer] This is somebody famous?

00:09:14.815 --> 00:09:15.648
- Yeah.

00:09:15.648 --> 00:09:16.770
- [Interviewer] Yeah. Don't name names.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.490
- Yeah, but it's really nice

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.550
'cause he's the only one
I've ever encountered

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:26.550
and just to find out that like
he does really raunchy shit.

00:09:26.552 --> 00:09:28.350
(Allison laughs)

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:29.370
- [Interviewer] So he's
not known as somebody

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:30.370
who would do this?

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:31.232
- No.

00:09:31.232 --> 00:09:32.830
(Allison laughs)

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:34.586
It just kind of sheds a
light on the other side.

00:09:34.586 --> 00:09:36.430
(Allison laughs)

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:37.830
- [Interviewer] Yeah, I think
there's probably some secrets

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.475
that some people have.

00:09:39.475 --> 00:09:40.690
- Oh yeah he has a lot of 'em.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:43.440
(Allison laughs)

00:09:44.995 --> 00:09:48.460
- [Interviewer] But what
you do to support yourself

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:53.460
does it change the way
you view people or men?

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.020
- It doesn't change the way I view anybody

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:59.023
because everyone has their vices.

00:10:01.666 --> 00:10:03.640
I'd be calling it kind of black if I did

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:08.640
but it has changed how
I'm able to interact

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.890
'cause now it's really hard
for me to be in a relationship

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:14.653
with a guy without being money involved.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:18.350
And it's hard for me to
see having sex with a guy

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:20.673
without some kind of exchange going.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:25.180
And it's really hurt me in that aspect

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.440
'cause I never had sex for the fun of it.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.680
It was always I was getting
something out of it.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:34.850
- [Interviewer] So far any
relationship that's just-

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.220
- Just love is hard.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:37.510
- [Interviewer] Nothing else?
- Yeah.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:39.320
- [Interviewer] Would
be difficult for you?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.153
- Yeah.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:44.100
- [Interviewer] You need the
money to make you feel loved?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:44.933
- I don't know-

00:10:44.933 --> 00:10:46.030
- [Interviewer] If it's for real?

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:49.063
- Yeah. And I don't like that.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.530
It's something that I really feel

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:52.770
like it has handicapped me.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:53.900
- [Interviewer] Yeah you've created it

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:55.847
by doing this for money.

00:10:55.847 --> 00:10:57.583
- And I created it all on my own.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.000
I'll just work through it.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.710
- [Interviewer] Did you have
dreams when you were young

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:08.065
of doing something with your life?

00:11:08.065 --> 00:11:08.898
- Yeah.

00:11:08.898 --> 00:11:10.420
- [Interviewer] What kind
of stuff did you envision?

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:13.210
- I was expecting to be
like graduating from school

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.393
like I wanted to be a
prosecuting attorney.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:19.720
And I tried to do everything
to like set that up,

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:21.910
but everything's just always fell through,

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.990
I was always moving,
I was never stationary

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.071
in one place for too long.

00:11:26.071 --> 00:11:27.173
- [Interviewer] So where you've ended up

00:11:27.173 --> 00:11:29.590
does that cause shame for you?

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.640
- It hasn't caused me shame
'cause I don't think of it

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:36.300
that way or else I'll get
like wrapped up in depression.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.900
I try to look at the
bright side of everything,

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.200
in that this is everything
I'm going through right now

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:45.700
is just gonna empower me, and
put me in a better situation,

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:50.700
but there is shame 'cause
I'm like almost I am 30

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.940
and I haven't done anything of my life.

00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:58.410
- [Interviewer] What was
the best time of your life?

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.823
- Best time of my life.

00:12:01.383 --> 00:12:04.970
It was pretty much when I
first came out of being trans

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:08.490
'cause I just felt like
I can capture the world.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.480
- [Interviewer] Was it liberating?

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:14.067
- Yeah, it was 'cause I finally
knew what was wrong with me.

00:12:14.067 --> 00:12:16.817
(Allison laughs)

00:12:18.804 --> 00:12:20.545
- [Interviewer] And do the
drugs make the situation

00:12:20.545 --> 00:12:22.860
more difficult for you?

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.590
- It hasn't made it more difficult

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.023
'cause it's my coping mechanism now.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:32.720
But when I lose weight
it does become a problem

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.560
because people automatically associate

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.760
that living where I live at with drugs,

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:40.520
it can never be anything other than that.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.420
But it probably has if you
probably talked to somebody

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:46.650
that knows me they
probably would say it has,

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.653
but I don't see how it has.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.337
- [Interviewer] Have
you been in love before?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.050
- Yeah, I was in a relationships
when I was a gay boy

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.500
but I haven't really been in one

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:01.710
since I tried getting in one
but he was okay with me working

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.890
and I didn't like that 'cause I felt like

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.140
he didn't respect me.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.900
And I keep on getting guys like that.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.700
They're okay with me working on the Blade.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.660
- [Interviewer] So you
would rather find somebody

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:12.493
who wasn't okay with that?

00:13:12.493 --> 00:13:14.350
- Wasn't okay with it.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.200
Yeah, 'cause then I felt like
you would actually love me.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.543
- [Interviewer] Where do you
think you'll be in five years?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.240
- Probably in the same spot.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.540
Hopefully going to school.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.030
But I really don't know.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.740
Everything's up in the air right now.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.130
- [Interviewer] Do you still
have contact with your family?

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.190
- Yeah. I talked to my mom.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:45.040
She recently moved to South Carolina

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:48.000
after my grandma died this year

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.073
so she's living with her third husband.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.300
Yeah, she's doing good.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:58.430
My brother is living with
her, he just had a baby.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:13:59.700
So she's dealing with a kid.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.660
So she's okay.

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:03.550
- [Interviewer] She accepts
your lifestyle and all that?

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.270
- Yeah, she didn't at first

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:07.410
and it wasn't that she didn't accept it

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:09.280
she didn't know how to
accept it 'cause she kept

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:12.830
on calling me my other name
and then (indistinct) her son

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:17.320
and I actually found out
earlier this year that she went

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.970
through a whole little phase where like,

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.350
she was stuck 'cause she
felt like she lost something

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.710
and she did, she lost her son.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.310
And I didn't understand
that for a really long time.

00:14:28.632 --> 00:14:30.810
But she really embraced having a daughter

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:34.913
and yeah, she's okay she's
probably my number one supporter.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:41.363
It hurts her that I haven't
been around her for so long.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.820
- [Interviewer] And how
do you define success?

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.820
But what would make you feel successful?

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:52.763
- By touching as many people as possible.

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:55.700
That's what I think is successful.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.773
Doing something that
impacts someone's life.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:03.750
And if you could do
that with so many people

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.733
you're successful.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.253
- [Interviewer] And what
would you say is the

00:15:09.253 --> 00:15:12.510
most important thing you've
learned in your 30 years?

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.817
- [Allison] Patience.

00:15:13.817 --> 00:15:15.570
(Allison deeply exhales)

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.640
That's probably the most important.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.290
I was never patient when I was a kid.

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:24.290
I always had to be right
now, and it's just patience.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.420
Everything will happen when
it's supposed to happen.

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.970
As long as you do the footwork.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.720
- [Interviewer] All right.
Well Allison thank you so much

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:34.879
for sharing your story.

00:15:34.879 --> 00:15:35.712
- Thank you.

00:15:35.712 --> 00:15:36.553
- [Interviewer] Very
nice getting to know you.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.660
I wish you the best of luck.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:39.493
- Thanks.

